---
import BaseLayout from "@layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Card from "@components/Card.astro";
import Button from "@components/Button.astro";
const title = 'SAP BTP Architecture Review & Boundary Audit - Jiandong Pei';
const description = 'Independent SAP BTP architecture review, Boundary Audit, and enterprise AI agent responsibility review for Clean Core extensions, identity, multitenancy, integration, lifecycle, and execution safety.';
---
<BaseLayout {title} {description}>
  <section class="stack tight">
    <h1>Work With Me</h1>
    <p class="measure">Independent architecture judgment for SAP BTP and enterprise AI decisions where local implementation success no longer proves that the structure is safe to evolve.</p>
    <p class="measure">This page is for fixed-scope external architecture judgment. If your organization is evaluating whether this capability belongs inside an internal architecture, platform, or AI governance team, see <a href="/for-architecture-teams/">For Architecture Teams</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="stack">
    <h2>When to engage</h2>
    <p class="measure">The right time is when the team can still make the system work, but no one can prove whether the architecture deserves to proceed as designed.</p>
    <div class="cards-grid">
      <Card title="SAP BTP extension decisions">
        <ul>
          <li>Postman works, Work Zone / AppRouter fails.</li>
          <li>One tenant works, the next tenant breaks.</li>
          <li>S/4 data has become shadow truth.</li>
          <li>Clean Core direction is approved, but extension responsibility remains unclear.</li>
          <li>The system runs, but lifecycle change requires manual repair.</li>
        </ul>
      </Card>
      <Card title="Enterprise AI decisions">
        <ul>
          <li>An agent can execute, but no one can prove whether it is safe to act.</li>
          <li>Agent, workflow, extension, and core-system responsibility is blurred.</li>
          <li>RAG, tools, workflow state, identity, and authorization are crossing boundaries.</li>
          <li>Prompt, tool, policy, model, or context changes cannot be reconstructed.</li>
        </ul>
      </Card>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cards-grid">
    <Card eyebrow="Strategic decision" title="Strategic Boundary Verdict" class="emphasis">
      <h3>Purpose</h3>
      <p class="measure">A focused independent verdict for Go / No-Go / Re-Architect decisions where a SAP BTP extension or AI architecture decision cannot converge.</p>
      <h3>Best for</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Urgent decision impasse.</li>
        <li>Protected-path failure such as AppRouter / Work Zone divergence.</li>
        <li>First signs of tenant rollout or lifecycle divergence.</li>
        <li>Executive-level need to classify whether the issue is structural.</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Deliverable</h3>
      <p class="measure">Boundary Verdict Memo with P1 structural risks, violated boundaries, and a Go / No-Go / Re-Architect direction. Typical duration: 5-7 business days.</p>
      <Button href="/contact/" variant="primary">Request boundary verdict</Button>
    </Card>

    <Card eyebrow="Audit" title="Full Boundary Audit">
      <h3>Purpose</h3>
      <p class="measure">A deeper architecture audit for SAP BTP landscapes that must survive long-term evolution, scale, governance, security hardening, and multi-tenant rollout.</p>
      <h3>Best for</h3>
      <p class="measure">Recurring incidents, fragmented ownership, vendor disagreement, rollout instability, or a landscape that must survive tenant, identity, data, integration, and lifecycle evolution.</p>
      <h3>Deliverable</h3>
      <p class="measure">Boundary risk matrix, failure-mode analysis, ownership/jurisdiction map, and final architectural verdict with non-implementation remediation direction.</p>
      <p class="measure">Typical duration: 2-3 calendar weeks.</p>
      <Button href="/contact/" variant="ghost">Request audit scope</Button>
    </Card>

    <Card eyebrow="Enterprise AI" title="Agent-Extension Responsibility Review">
      <h3>Purpose</h3>
      <p class="measure">To determine whether an SAP Joule, enterprise AI, workflow, or agent initiative has clearly assigned responsibility across agents, governed tools, extension APIs, workflows, assistants, and core systems.</p>
      <h3>Typical questions</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Should this be an agent, an extension, a workflow, or automation?</li>
        <li>What business truth is involved?</li>
        <li>What can the agent execute?</li>
        <li>Which workflow contains accountability?</li>
        <li>Which extension APIs or governed tools should be invoked?</li>
        <li>Which system owns final state?</li>
        <li>How will prompts, tools, policies, workflows, context, and extension APIs evolve?</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Deliverable</h3>
      <p class="measure">Responsibility Boundary Memo with a responsibility map, ambiguity areas, truth / execution / lifecycle / accountability risks, and recommended architecture direction.</p>
      <Button href="/contact/" variant="ghost">Assess responsibility boundaries</Button>
    </Card>

    <Card eyebrow="Authority" title="Architecture Verdict Authority">
      <h3>Purpose</h3>
      <p class="measure">Programs where a single architectural misjudgment would create disproportionate long-term cost and recurring external arbitration is needed.</p>
      <h3>Deliverable</h3>
      <p class="measure">Periodic boundary health reviews, pre-validation of major architectural changes, and limited emergency architectural arbitration.</p>
      <Button href="/contact/" variant="ghost">Send structured summary</Button>
    </Card>
  </section>

  <section class="stack">
    <h2>Why this is different from implementation review</h2>
    <p class="measure">Implementation reviews validate local correctness; boundary work establishes whether the architecture is still legitimate across responsibility, runtime, identity, tenant, data, integration, and lifecycle boundaries.</p>
    <p class="measure">The question is not whether a capable team can keep the initiative moving. The question is whether the current structure deserves to continue as designed.</p>
    <p class="measure">This preserves independence. Delivery teams implement; this service judges whether the architecture deserves to proceed.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="stack">
    <h2>Out of scope</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Not implementation work.</li>
      <li>Not configuration work.</li>
      <li>Not production code maintenance.</li>
      <li>Not staff augmentation.</li>
      <li>Not project management.</li>
      <li>Not delivery team replacement.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="stack">
    <h2>Initiation protocol</h2>
    <p class="measure">Send one structured page. That is enough to determine whether the work is an agent-extension responsibility review, strategic verdict, full audit, or verdict authority format.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Landscape — S/4, BTP runtimes, entry surfaces, identity</li>
      <li>Divergence — by tenant, path, surface, agent behavior, or workflow state</li>
      <li>Timeline — go-live, rollout, recent change, AI pilot, model/tool change</li>
      <li>Ownership — who holds truth, action, state, lifecycle, and accountability today</li>
      <li>Decision — the choice that cannot converge</li>
    </ul>
    <div style="display:flex; gap:.75rem; flex-wrap:wrap;">
      <Button href="/contact/" variant="primary">Send structured summary</Button>
      <Button href="/intake-template/" variant="ghost">Use intake template</Button>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="stack">
    <h2>Related reading and SEO entry pages</h2>
    <p class="measure">These pages explain common situations and architecture models. The actual engagement format is determined after the one-page summary, usually as a Strategic Boundary Verdict, Full Boundary Audit, Agent-Extension Responsibility Review, or Architecture Verdict Authority path.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/agent-extension-boundary-model/">Agent-Extension Boundary Model</a></li>
      <li><a href="/sap-agent-extension-workflow/">Should this be an SAP agent, extension, or workflow?</a></li>
      <li><a href="/sap-btp-architecture-review/">SAP BTP Architecture Review</a></li>
      <li><a href="/sap-btp-extension-audit/">SAP BTP Extension Audit</a></li>
      <li><a href="/sap-btp-post-go-live-failure-assessment/">SAP BTP Post-Go-Live Failure Assessment</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
